# Secrets — never commit. Template lives in .env.example
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local scratch
*.log
node_modules/

# Course material (Interview Kickstart's copyright — not redistributed; README summarises the brief).
# Pattern, not two filenames: the template PDF sat tracked for months because the original
# rule named only file 05, and nobody adds the next one to a list of exact names.
docs/0*_Official_*.pdf

# Build artefact — duplicates n8n/workflows/; regenerate with Compress-Archive for Drive uploads
salesgenie-n8n-workflows.zip

# Demo video working files — large/intermediate, never committed. Final small
# exports (teaser gif/mp4) are committed explicitly from exports/.
presentation/video-assets/raw/
presentation/video-assets/audio/
presentation/video-assets/work/

# Finished cuts are tens of MB — they ship as GitHub release assets, not in git
# history, so a clone stays small. Un-ignore explicitly (git add -f) if a small
# teaser ever needs committing.
presentation/video-assets/exports/*.mp4

# Production scaffolding for the video and the live talk, kept locally but not
# published (2026-08-10). These describe how to FILM the system, not how it
# works: shot lists, teleprompter, take-by-take scripts, narration tooling for an
# approach that was abandoned. Six of them opened by declaring themselves
# superseded, which made presentation/ read as a graveyard of retracted plans.
presentation/video-assets/
presentation/visuals/
presentation/demo-deck-for-presenter.html
presentation/hero-demo-runbook.md
presentation/new-business-script.md
presentation/video-script.md
presentation/design-handoff-prompt.md
presentation/slides-content.md
presentation/explainer.md

# A learning log written in the third person about the author's own gaps, beside
# work meant to be judged on its merits. Kept locally; the workflow explanations
# it contains are covered by docs/workflow-tour.md and presentation/deck.html.
learning/

# Output of scripts/retarget-host.js — someone else's host baked into copies of the
# exports. Personal to whoever ran it; regenerate rather than commit.
n8n/workflows-retargeted/
